{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793314873,"nonce":"lIxa7pXTjdU1mQ4synUDrC8JEOU=","title":"pull, push and sync carry only the work-* namespaces; migrate --from REMOTE fetches git-bug's","message":"`git work pull`/`push`/`sync` iterate every subcache, so they still fetch, merge and push the frozen `refs/issues/*` through the bug subcache.\nNo saved refspec covers that namespace, so `git remote prune origin` (Luis's `git sync`) prunes `refs/remotes/origin/issues/*` on every run through `+refs/heads/*`, and the next `git work sync` brings them back.\n\nDecided 2026-10-29 (Luis): the legacy namespaces leave the default sync. Fetching them is opt-in and belongs to the one command that reads them: `git work migrate --from REMOTE` fetches and merges `refs/issues/*` and `refs/identities/*` from that remote, then migrates as it does today.\nWhy migrate and not a `--legacy` flag on pull/push/sync: the frozen store is only read in order to import it, so nothing should push it again, and a flag on three commands would extend a store that is being deleted (860d6e0), as the kind of sugar flag `doc/design/cli-convention.md` argues against.\nThe bug subcache stays registered for local reads (`git work bug`) until the deletion round.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core","cli"],"status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}